{%- comment -%}
  LBASS HERO — CTA COLOUR DEFAULTS (2026-07-31)
  Rendered from snippets/lbass-hero-fx.liquid.

  THE BUG THIS FIXES. The section wrote its CTA colours as inline custom
  properties on <header>:
      style="--cta-bg:{{ section.settings.cta_bg }}; ..."
  When a colour setting is UNSET, Liquid renders nothing, so the browser
  receives:
      --cta-bg:;
  That is not "undefined" — it is DEFINED AND EMPTY. `var(--cta-bg,#BF2E15)`
  only uses its fallback when the property is undefined, so the empty value won
  and the primary button rendered fully TRANSPARENT (measured
  rgba(0,0,0,0)) on a hero whose whole job is that one click.

  Two-part fix: the section now emits each property ONLY when the setting has a
  value, and the defaults below sit on `.lbh` so the button is always painted
  even if every setting is blank. Belt and braces — a hero CTA must never be
  able to disappear.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
.lbh{ --cta-bg:#BF2E15; --cta-fg:#FFFFFF; --cta-bg-hover:#8F1F0D; }
</style>
